Table full name: mitelman-db.prod.MolClinGene
Column name: MolClin Type: STRING Description: flag indicating either molecular 'M', or clinical 'C'
Column name: RefNo Type: INT64 Description: reference number, eg '15563'
Column name: InvNo Type: INT64 Description: investigation number, usually between 1 and 10
Column name: OrderNo Type: INT64 Description: order number, between 1 and 15
Column name: Prefix Type: STRING Description: prefix string -- either blank or '+' 
Column name: Gene Type: STRING Description: gene symbol(s), eg 'KMT2A' or 'BCR/ABL1'
Column name: Suffix Type: STRING Description: suffix string -- either blank or '+'
Sample rows:
[{'MolClin': 'C', 'RefNo': 3967, 'InvNo': 1, 'OrderNo': 1, 'Prefix': None, 'Gene': 'BCR::ABL1', 'Suffix': None}, {'MolClin': 'C', 'RefNo': 3976, 'InvNo': 1, 'OrderNo': 1, 'Prefix': None, 'Gene': 'BCR::ABL1', 'Suffix': None}, {'MolClin': 'C', 'RefNo': 3976, 'InvNo': 2, 'OrderNo': 1, 'Prefix': None, 'Gene': 'BCR::ABL1', 'Suffix': None}, {'MolClin': 'C', 'RefNo': 4541, 'InvNo': 1, 'OrderNo': 1, 'Prefix': None, 'Gene': 'PML::RARA', 'Suffix': None}, {'MolClin': 'C', 'RefNo': 4624, 'InvNo': 1, 'OrderNo': 1, 'Prefix': None, 'Gene': 'BCR::ABL1', 'Suffix': None}]

--------------------------------------------------
Table full name: mitelman-db.prod.RecurrentData
Column name: Chromosome Type: STRING Description: chromosome number (1- 22, X or Y)
Column name: Arm Type: STRING Description: arm of the chromosome (p or q)
Column name: Band Type: STRING Description: position of the gene on the p or q arm
Column name: Abnormality Type: STRING Description: abnormality description, eg 'add(19)(q13)' or 'del(20)(q11q13)'
Column name: Morph Type: STRING Description: morphology code, eg '1602'
Column name: Topo Type: STRING Description: topography code, eg '0902' (or blank)
Column name: TotalCases Type: STRING Description: total number of cases (up to 2150)
Column name: Gene Type: STRING Description: gene symbol(s), eg 'KMT2A+' or 'BCR/ABL1' or blank
Column name: ChrOrder Type: INT64 Description: numeric order of the chromosome
Column name: Type Type: STRING Description: indicate balanced ('B') or unbalanced ('U')
Sample rows:
[{'Chromosome': 'Y', 'Arm': 'q', 'Band': '10', 'Abnormality': 'i(Y)(q10)', 'Morph': '1820', 'Topo': None, 'TotalCases': '2', 'Gene': None, 'ChrOrder': 24, 'Type': 'U'}, {'Chromosome': '1', 'Arm': 'q', 'Band': '10', 'Abnormality': 'der(1;2)(q10;p10)', 'Morph': '1702', 'Topo': None, 'TotalCases': '2', 'Gene': None, 'ChrOrder': 1, 'Type': 'U'}, {'Chromosome': '1', 'Arm': 'q', 'Band': '10', 'Abnormality': 'der(1;2)(q10;q10)', 'Morph': '8804', 'Topo': '0801', 'TotalCases': '2', 'Gene': None, 'ChrOrder': 1, 'Type': 'U'}, {'Chromosome': '1', 'Arm': 'q', 'Band': '10', 'Abnormality': 'der(1;3)(q10;q10)', 'Morph': '1702', 'Topo': None, 'TotalCases': '2', 'Gene': None, 'ChrOrder': 1, 'Type': 'U'}, {'Chromosome': '1', 'Arm': 'q', 'Band': '10', 'Abnormality': 'der(1;3)(q10;q10)', 'Morph': '3111', 'Topo': '0401', 'TotalCases': '2', 'Gene': None, 'ChrOrder': 1, 'Type': 'U'}]

--------------------------------------------------
Table full name: mitelman-db.prod.KaryAbnorm
Column name: RefNo Type: INT64 Description: reference number, eg '14620'
Column name: CaseNo Type: STRING Description: case number, most frequently an integer between 1 and 10, but can also be an arbitrary string, eg '11H046'
Column name: InvNo Type: INT64 Description: investigation number (between 1 and 9)
Column name: CloneNo Type: INT64 Description: clone number (between 1 and 58)
Column name: OrderNo Type: INT64 Description: order number (between 1 and 198)
Column name: Abnormality Type: STRING Description: eg '46', or 'XY', or 'XX', or '-22', etc
Sample rows:
[{'RefNo': 401, 'CaseNo': '109', 'InvNo': 1, 'CloneNo': 1, 'OrderNo': 1, 'Abnormality': '??'}, {'RefNo': 737, 'CaseNo': '105', 'InvNo': 1, 'CloneNo': 1, 'OrderNo': 1, 'Abnormality': '??'}, {'RefNo': 737, 'CaseNo': '124', 'InvNo': 1, 'CloneNo': 1, 'OrderNo': 1, 'Abnormality': '??'}, {'RefNo': 737, 'CaseNo': '63', 'InvNo': 1, 'CloneNo': 1, 'OrderNo': 1, 'Abnormality': '??'}, {'RefNo': 737, 'CaseNo': '66', 'InvNo': 1, 'CloneNo': 1, 'OrderNo': 1, 'Abnormality': '??'}]

